I don't hold with the attitude that savescumming is inherently evil --
it's especially an interesting way to explore how certain games would
turn out if you take different actions from different points, and hey,
it's a game anyway, so if playing that way makes it more fun for you,
by all means, go for it.

However, I might suggest that there a good number of ways to end a
game in style other than ascending. Sure, you haven't *beat* the game
without ascending, but then again, there are a wide variety of
challenges you really haven't necessarily met even if you ascend. So,
if this particular wizard you're playing can't get the Eye or the
Bell? You haven't exactly *lost* the game if your wizard levels up to
some nice level and escapes the dungeon with a few artifacts, some
wishes, a fortune in gold, and a pet ki-rin. Raid the castle and
Gehennom and Ludios if it's there, kill Vlad and the Wizard, go home,
crack open a few !oBooze....




